summary:
  The popup's backfill sends the logo hunt to a station's homepage on a
  metered connection too.

history:
  A homepage hunt reads up to half a megabyte of page and up to twelve
  pictures of as much again, with no click. The directory's own byuuid answer
  is a few hundred bytes, which is why the backfill asked it on any link; the
  hunt waits for one that is not metered.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
              if (fav !== "" || home === "" || NetworkInformation.isMetered) done(fav);

replace:
              if (fav !== "" || home === "") done(fav);

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_the_popup_reads_a_homepage_only_through_the_guarded_hunt.
  Line-neutral.
